# Base URL of the API.
#
# Leave this EMPTY in both development and production.
#
#   Development — vite.config.js proxies /api to http://localhost:4000.
#   Production  — vercel.json rewrites /api to the Railway service.
#
# Either way the browser sees a single origin, which is what keeps the refresh
# token a first-party cookie. Pointing this straight at the API domain instead
# would make it a third-party cookie: Safari blocks those by default, so sign-in
# would appear to work and then drop the session on the next page load.
VITE_API_URL=
